How to add a new test suite?

Lets take the example of ViewLayout test suite.

- Create ViewLayout.test.ts
- Add license header
- Add the root level describe:

  describe('ViewLayout', function() {

        // Write all tests inside this block.

  });

- Write all test code inside the root level describe function block.

- Pull in all the necessary typescript source code in ** sources.ts ** for which the tests are written.

  /// <reference path="../src/app/ViewLayout.ts" />
  /// <reference path="../src/app/ViewLayoutMultiPage.ts" />
  /// <reference path="../src/app/LayoutingService.ts" />

- Finally add reference the test file ViewLayout.test.ts in ** main.ts **

  /// <reference path="./ViewLayout.test.ts" />

Now to run this newly created test suite, run from browser/ dir:

$ touch mocha_tests/main.ts && make build-tests && npm run test-single ViewLayout

Testing against the real page

A test that needs the map, the dialogs or anything else the running page sets up can load the
built page itself, rather than build a stand-in for the map:

    let page: DocumentPage;
    before(async function () {
        this.timeout(60000);
        page = await openDocumentPage('text');
        page.serverSays('perm: edit');
    });
    after(function () {
        page.close();
    });

openDocumentPage() loads dist/cool.html with all its scripts and plays the server's side of a
document load, so page.map is the real map with a real document layer. page.serverSays() sends
a message from the server, and page.sent holds what the page sent. A page takes a second or two
to load, so a suite loads one in before() and shares it between its tests.
CollabNotices.test.ts is an example. It needs a built dist, which "make check" builds first.
